* Canon: bags/lararium/ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/founding-runbook.mem:82 and any .mem/.md under bags/ or CLAUDE.md naming `observe/daemon` or `observeDaemon` (`grep -rn "observe/daemon\|observeDaemon\|daemon-observe" bags CLAUDE.md`): true the text to the face canon mirror; reseal each touched .mem with `node packages/lares-cli/bin/lares.mjs meme normalize <file>`.

TESTS: after the edits, `grep -rn "daemon-observe\|observeDaemon\|OBSERVE_DIR\|isObserveProjectionPath\|daemonObserveRoot" packages tools bags CLAUDE.md` (excluding dist and node_modules) returns nothing. Build + stamp each touched package (`pnpm --filter <pkg> build && node tools/stamp-build.mjs . --pkg <short>`), typecheck each, run each touched package's directly affected test files, then the full lares-cli and lararium-node suites one at a time with `--maxWorkers=4` (stop a run that shows no output for 15 minutes and report the last file). `node tools/evergreen-boundary.mjs`, `tools/placement-residency-witness.sh`, `bash tools/bcc-witness.sh` if a .mem changed. Failures reading `secret-home-unavailable` belong to another seat: count them apart.

LIMITS: only retirement edits; do not touch Keyhive, commands/init.ts, the found path, or the control-document code. No git commit, no push, no stash. Never touch ~/.lares or docker.

